## Proposed Technical Changes

### 1. Database Connection Pooling & Fast Execution
#### [MODIFY] [read_executor.py](file:///c:/Users/nayak_o7hopi6/Desktop/Agent/app/database/read_executor.py)
- Replace per-request `pymysql.connect()` with a persistent SQLAlchemy engine connection pool (`pool_size=10`, `max_overflow=20`, `pool_recycle=3600`, `pool_pre_ping=True`).
- Eliminate TCP connection setup latency (reduces DB overhead from ~150ms to <10ms).

---

### 2. In-Memory Schema Caching, Relationship Graph & Intent Retrieval
#### [MODIFY] [retriever.py](file:///c:/Users/nayak_o7hopi6/Desktop/Agent/app/retriever/retriever.py)
- Load schema metadata into memory on startup (`@functools.lru_cache`). Avoid disk/ChromaDB queries on every request.
- Implement Smart Intent Detection using keyword matching to pull ONLY relevant table cards.
- Build an in-memory **Relationship Graph** (`users.id` -> `wallet_transaction.user_id`, etc.) for instant join resolution.
- Enforce strict chunk limits: maximum 3 schema cards, 2 SQL syntax patterns.

---

### 3. Query Pattern & Exact Match Caching
#### [MODIFY] [sql_agent.py](file:///c:/Users/nayak_o7hopi6/Desktop/Agent/app/agent/sql_agent.py)
- **Exact Match Cache**: Store normalized user prompts -> SQL queries. Repeat queries return in <5ms.
- **Pattern Date Submitter**: Recognize date range query templates (e.g. "Show July wallet transactions" vs "Show August wallet transactions") and swap date bounds without calling LLM (0ms LLM overhead!).
- Execute retrieval, ambiguity check, and AST validation in parallel using `concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor`.

---

